\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 Step 1: Define your gRPC service contract (proto file)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is the most important design step \'97 it forces you to think about your API before writing logic.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 proto/kv.proto
\f2\fs24 :\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 syntax = "proto3";\
\
package kvstore;\
\
service KeyValueStore \{\
  rpc Put(PutRequest) returns (PutResponse);\
  rpc Get(GetRequest) returns (GetResponse);\
  rpc Delete(DeleteRequest) returns (DeleteResponse);\
\}\
\
message PutRequest \{\
  string key = 1;\
  bytes value = 2;\
\}\
\
message PutResponse \{\
  bool success = 1;\
\}\
\
message GetRequest \{\
  string key = 1;\
\}\
\
message GetResponse \{\
  bool found = 1;\
  bytes value = 2;\
\}\
\
message DeleteRequest \{\
  string key = 1;\
\}\
\
message DeleteResponse \{\
  bool success = 1;\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 Why 
\f4\fs26 bytes
\f2\fs24  for value instead of 
\f4\fs26 string
\f2\fs24 ? KV stores should be content-agnostic \'97 values could be arbitrary binary blobs, not just text.\
Don't add replication/versioning fields yet (no vector clocks, no node IDs). Keep Phase 1 dumb and simple \'97 you'll extend this proto in later phases.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

